  "requirement": "Every JSON file directly under `evidence/` MUST correspond to a declared requirement or named example. A JSON file at `evidence/rust/<rust_file>.json` MUST correspond to a first-party Rust source file containing an explicitly declared function or method. Habeas MUST report evidence JSON files in other locations under `evidence/` and Rust evidence files or entries whose source item no longer exists.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The implementation covers only the first part of `requirements.ci.orphans`. The Rust evidence part is not implemented, and the code and tests contradict it.\n\n**What is implemented and tested.** The `{impl}` loop in `src/evidence.rs` (`inspect_repository_with_progress`, from about line 121) walks every JSON file under `evidence/`. Only a file directly under `evidence/` whose stem matches a non-term requirement or example is accepted. Anything else gets `\"<label>: no matching requirement or example\"`. Three tests cover this:\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks the `ghost.json` orphan.\n- `nested_evidence_files_are_reported` checks `evidence/nested/rules.ready.json`.\n- The `fixture` helper in `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` builds the project those tests use.\n\n**What is missing.** The requirement also says:\n- A JSON file at `evidence/rust/<rust_file>.json` MUST correspond to a first-party Rust source file containing an explicitly declared function or method.\n- Habeas MUST report Rust evidence files or entries whose source item no longer exists.\n\nThe code has no handling for `evidence/rust/` files:\n- A search of `src` finds no handling of an `\"rust\"` evidence directory or of stale Rust evidence entries.\n- The loop treats every file under `evidence/rust/` as an ordinary file.\n- Any such file is reported as `no matching requirement or example`, even if it names an existing Rust source file with a declared function.\n- No code checks whether the Rust file exists, whether it contains a declared function or method, or whether a recorded item is stale.\n\nThe tests confirm the gap. `nested_evidence_files_are_reported` asserts that `evidence/rust/src/lib.rs.json` is an orphan. Other tests assert that `evidence/rust` does not exist (`tests/authoring_batch.rs:462`, `tests/commands.rs:763` and `tests/commands.rs:899`). Nothing tests a valid Rust evidence file being accepted, a Rust evidence file for a missing source file, or a stale Rust entry.\n\nThe requirement text in `md/requirements/ci.md` still describes the `evidence/rust` behavior, so the code and tests have diverged from it. No FIXME acknowledges this gap, so the judgment is false rather than FIXME.",
